course: dictionary
lesson: 12529
title: Desperation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Desperation is a noun for the feeling of having almost no hope left. When you feel desperate, you are willing to try anything, even something risky.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «In desperation, Mia climbed the tall tree to reach her lost kite.» Mia has no other way to get her kite back, and climbing a tree is risky, so the words in desperation tell you she had no better choice.
explain: Ask yourself: has the character run out of hope? If they have, and they try something wild, desperation is the word that fits. Swap it into the sentence to check that the meaning still makes sense.
fact: Desperation means the feeling of having almost no hope.
fact: A person in desperation is willing to try anything, even something risky.
fact: «In desperation» and «out of desperation» are common phrases in stories.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad in desperation escapes from prison dressed as a washerwoman.
fact: Desperation is an uncountable noun, so we say «desperation», not «a desperation».
exercise: «The lost puppy ran through the town in desperation, searching for its family.» What does in desperation show? | *The puppy had almost no hope left | The puppy was sleeping peacefully | The puppy had just been given a bath | The puppy was very happy and playful
exercise: Which word means the feeling of having almost no hope? | *Desperation | Happiness | Curiosity | Boredom
exercise: «In desperation, he sold his bike to buy a ticket home.» Why did he sell his bike? | He was bored of cycling | He lost the bike in a game | He wanted a new bike | *He had no better choice left
test: «With no food left and no one to ask, Sam ate the strange berries in desperation.» Which word names the feeling behind this action? | Joy | Calm | Surprise | *Desperation
test: Which sentence shows a character trying something risky because there is no hope left? | The cat slept on the warm mat. | Grandma baked a cake for the party. | The bus arrived on time. | *Out of desperation, the explorer crossed the icy river on a fallen log.
exam: Which best explains desperation? | Feeling sure that everything will go well | Feeling bored and wanting something to do | *Having almost no hope, so willing to try anything, even something risky | Feeling very proud of a good score
